      locationAudio = "dungeon",
      url = ""
    },
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Lucien-14, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual image input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents; do not borrow its subjects or locations. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Lord Lucien [Cutout].webp` as Lord Lucien’s exact identity reference and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as post-Embrace Fomórach’s exact identity reference. Preserve their faces, apparent ages, builds, relative stature, hair, complexion, and distinguishing anatomy while adapting clothing and grooming to 1955–1958. Also attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Obfuscate Invisibility).png` and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Mask of 1000 Faces).png` as visual-language references only.\n\nOBFUSCATE LANGUAGE — Use an Obfuscate effect only where a quad explicitly requests it. “Concealment” means Fomórach’s true form remains visible to the privileged audience, but selected contour regions dissolve into unfinished charcoal hatching and blank negative space borrowing the background texture, matching the Obfuscate Invisibility reference; keep most of him solid and recognizable, without a colored aura. “Mask” means his true form remains visible to the privileged audience while exactly one faint, translucent, ordinary human face and body are aligned over the same pose like a double exposure, matching the Mask of 1000 Faces reference; it is one superimposed perceptual shell, not a second person. Nearby mortals simply keep their attention elsewhere; do not build elaborate eyeline choreography around proving the effect.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1955–1958, the Mojave Desert, USA. Lucien is recovering from decades of torpor: in early moments he is corpselike, pale, gaunt, dry-skinned, hollow-cheeked, and desperately hungry; recovery may gradually restore his elegant slim build and blond curls. Fomórach is a massive, severely deformed Nosferatu whose controlled vigilance contrasts with Lucien’s weakness. Keep every scene at night or inside a completely sunless shelter. Every quad must depict both Lord Lucien and Fomórach. Clothing, vehicles, architecture, tools, and infrastructure must be period-appropriate.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe and render only what one camera can see in one instant. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful camera variation without obscuring anatomy or interaction. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in each quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, romantic posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt a remote Mojave excavation beneath a black 1950s desert sky, Fomórach is kneeling at the rim of a rough opened grave and is tipping an ordinary small transparent glass bottle directly above Lucien. One clean narrow stream of dark red liquid is visibly falling from its open neck into Lucien's mouth. Lucien is half-risen from the earth with both hands gripping the grave rim, his head fully tilted back and his open fanged mouth directly beneath the stream. His body is skeletal, caked with soil, severely haggard and desiccated; his golden curls are filthy, tangled, flattened and matted, while his wide eyes and rigid jaw are showing overpowering hunger. Fomórach is watching Lucien with tense concentration while wearing dusty excavation workwear: a coarse work shirt with rolled sleeves, worn field jacket, rugged trousers and scuffed boots. Canvas work lights, digging tools, rope, disturbed earth and a military-surplus truck are surrounding them. The camera is low inside the grave beside Lucien's shoulder, looking upward toward both men.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside an abandoned mining shack at night, Lucien is sitting weakly on a cot beneath a blanket while Fomórach is kneeling several feet away and is sliding a sealed blood bottle across the plank floor toward him with one extended hand. Lucien’s gaunt face is turned toward the bottle, his lips parted around visible fangs and his fingers digging into the cot edge as he resists lunging. Fomórach’s broad body is braced and ready, his eyes fixed on Lucien. A lantern, old ore maps, boarded windows, rusted tools, and moonlit machinery are framing the tense distance between them. Use a floor-level camera beside the bottle.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nAt Fomórach’s isolated desert search camp at night, the recovering Lucien is standing unsteadily beside a canvas tent in borrowed 1950s clothing while Fomórach is fastening a heavy travel cloak around Lucien’s shoulders. Lucien is looking down at a road map spread across the hood of their battered truck, his hollow face alert but exhausted; Fomórach is looking at the approaching glow of distant headlights beyond the camp. Water cans, bedrolls, digging tools, and black mountains establish weeks of survival. Use an elevated three-quarter view over the map and truck hood.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a lonely desert highway inspection point at night, Lucien is leaning against the open driver-side door and is handing forged papers to a uniformed patrolman with a thin, strained version of his usual charming smile. Fomórach is standing immediately behind the car with one hand on the packed trunk, using concealment: his true monstrous body is visible to the audience while the edges of his coat and shoulders are dissolving into charcoal hatching and borrowed desert darkness. The patrolman is studying the papers rather than Fomórach. Lucien is glancing toward Fomórach from the corner of his eye. Headlamps, windblown sand, a road barrier, and distant military lights are defining the scene.",
