    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Lucien-15, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual image input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents; do not borrow its subjects or locations. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Lord Lucien [Cutout].webp` as Lord Lucien’s exact identity reference and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as post-Embrace Fomórach’s exact identity reference. Preserve their faces, apparent ages, builds, relative stature, hair, complexion, and distinguishing anatomy while adapting clothing and grooming to 1958–1962. Also attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Obfuscate Invisibility).png` and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Mask of 1000 Faces).png` as visual-language references only.\n\nOBFUSCATE LANGUAGE — Use an Obfuscate effect only where a quad explicitly requests it. “Concealment” means Fomórach’s true form remains visible to the privileged audience, but selected contour regions dissolve into unfinished charcoal hatching and blank negative space borrowing the background texture, matching the Obfuscate Invisibility reference; keep most of him solid and recognizable, without a colored aura. “Mask” means his true form remains visible to the privileged audience while exactly one faint, translucent, ordinary human face and body are aligned over the same pose like a double exposure, matching the Mask of 1000 Faces reference; it is one superimposed perceptual shell, not a second person. Nearby mortals simply keep their attention elsewhere; do not build elaborate eyeline choreography around proving the effect.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1958–1962, the southern United States. Lucien is again outwardly elegant, slim, blond, and socially magnetic; in public he uses an amused half-smile and confident conversational gestures. Fomórach is a massive, severely deformed Nosferatu, guarded and practical. Their evolving reliance should read through coordinated action rather than intimacy. All scenes are at night or in sealed sunless interiors. Every quad must depict both Lord Lucien and Fomórach. Clothing, vehicles, architecture, tools, and infrastructure must be period-appropriate.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe and render only what one camera can see in one instant. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful camera variation without obscuring anatomy or interaction. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in each quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, romantic posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nUnder harsh white service lights at a rain-heavy small-town gas station, Lucien is leaning casually against the open hood of their late-1950s automobile and is offering forged registration papers to a suspicious patrol officer with an easy cocky smile. Fomórach is crouching beside the rear wheel with a jack handle in one hand, using concealment: most of his true form is sharply visible to the audience while his outer contours dissolve into charcoal hatching and the garage shadows. An attendant is bent over the smoking engine and is not looking toward Fomórach. Use an over-the-shoulder camera from behind the patrol officer, with wet pumps and red tail-light reflections behind the pair.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a modest neon motor-court office at night, Lucien is placing folded cash on the counter while smiling toward a tired clerk. Fomórach is standing beside him with one hand holding a worn suitcase, using Mask of a Thousand Faces: one faint ordinary middle-aged traveller in a plain 1960 suit is precisely superimposed over Fomórach’s same pose, while his true deformed face and massive body remain visible beneath to the audience. The clerk is looking at Lucien. Lucien is giving Fomórach a quick sideways glance. A key rack, desk bell, rain-streaked glass, and parked finned car fill the frame. Camera just behind the clerk’s shoulder.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn an all-night southern diner, Lucien and Fomórach are sitting opposite one another in a vinyl booth while a waitress is setting down two coffee cups. Lucien is smiling up at the waitress and holding a folded route map flat with one hand. Fomórach is using Mask of a Thousand Faces; an aligned translucent shell of an unremarkable travelling salesman overlays his true Nosferatu form as he points one finger at their next highway turn. The waitress’s attention remains on Lucien. Freight trucks and rain are visible through the windows. Use a low tabletop camera with the map in the foreground.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a secluded roadside camp beneath southern pines at night, Lucien and Fomórach are facing one another across the open trunk of their late-1950s car with no mortals nearby and no Obfuscate effect. Lucien is holding a forged identity card between two fingers, his brows raised and his half-smile challenging; Fomórach is pressing one broad finger onto a route map laid across the luggage, his jaw set and eyes narrowed toward Lucien. Blood bottles, canned provisions, bedrolls, drying clothes, and improvised daylight coverings are packed around the focal exchange. The scene contains no lantern, firepit, flame, ember, or firelight. Cold blue-white moonlight and restrained crimson light from the car's rear tail lights illuminate both figures, the trunk supplies, and reflective black paint. Use a restrained Dutch angle from inside the trunk.",
