    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Lucien-16, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual image input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents; do not borrow its subjects or locations. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Lord Lucien [Cutout].webp` as Lord Lucien’s exact identity reference and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as post-Embrace Fomórach’s exact identity reference. Preserve their faces, apparent ages, builds, relative stature, hair, complexion, and distinguishing anatomy while adapting clothing and grooming to 1962–1967. Also attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Obfuscate Invisibility).png` and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Mask of 1000 Faces).png` as visual-language references only.\n\nOBFUSCATE LANGUAGE — Use an Obfuscate effect only where a quad explicitly requests it. “Concealment” means Fomórach’s true form remains visible to the privileged audience, but selected contour regions dissolve into unfinished charcoal hatching and blank negative space borrowing the background texture, matching the Obfuscate Invisibility reference; keep most of him solid and recognizable, without a colored aura. “Mask” means his true form remains visible to the privileged audience while exactly one faint, translucent, ordinary human face and body are aligned over the same pose like a double exposure, matching the Mask of 1000 Faces reference; it is one superimposed perceptual shell, not a second person. Nearby mortals simply keep their attention elsewhere; do not build elaborate eyeline choreography around proving the effect.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1962–1967, the northern United States and Great Lakes corridor. Lucien is elegant, slim, blond, and socially fearless, answering pressure with a self-assured half-smile. Fomórach is a massive, severely deformed Nosferatu, wary and physically grounded. Rain, snow, industrial light, freight infrastructure, and tightening border controls define this leg of the journey. All scenes are at night or within a sealed sunless interior. Every quad must depict both Lord Lucien and Fomórach. Clothing, vehicles, architecture, tools, and infrastructure must be period-appropriate.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe and render only what one camera can see in one instant. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful camera variation without obscuring anatomy or interaction. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in each quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, romantic posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a rain-slick Great Lakes motor-court parking lot at night, Lucien is holding an umbrella over an open paper map on the car roof while Fomórach is changing a flat tyre beside him. Lucien is pointing to a northern route and looking down toward Fomórach with an encouraging half-smile; Fomórach is gripping the wheel wrench and glaring at the damaged tyre. No mortals are nearby and no Obfuscate is active. Brick cabins, dark lake water, freight lights, and cold rain surround them. Use a high three-quarter camera that keeps both men and the map legible.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAt a Great Lakes industrial waterfront at night, Lucien is standing lookout beside stacked freight crates while Fomórach is forcing a rusted warehouse door upward with both hands. Lucien’s head is turned toward an approaching security vehicle, his smile gone and his posture suddenly alert; Fomórach is looking into the opening beneath the door, his broad frame straining. No mortals are close enough to require Obfuscate. Wet rails, cranes, freight cars, smokestacks, and reflected red signal lights create deep perspective. Use a low camera near the rising door.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside an all-night roadside restaurant beside a northern interstate, Lucien is leaning across a Formica booth and is charming a uniformed local official with a relaxed smile while holding their route map partly folded. Fomórach is seated beside Lucien using Mask of a Thousand Faces; one translucent, ordinary broad-shouldered traveller is aligned exactly over his true monstrous form. Fomórach is watching the official’s badge with a guarded expression while the official’s attention stays on Lucien. Payphones, truck lights, and rain-streaked windows frame the booth. Use a camera from the empty opposite seat.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a rain-darkened 1960s border customs station at night, Lucien is seated naturally in the driver’s seat of their sedan and is extending travel papers through the open window to a suspicious officer with a confident conversational smile. Fomórach is fully seated in the front passenger seat—torso, hips, both legs, and feet correctly placed inside the compartment—using concealment: his true form remains visible to the audience while charcoal-negative-space dissolution breaks up his outer silhouette against the dark upholstery. He is watching Lucien rather than the officer. Barriers, booths, inspection lights, wet pavement, and an industrial river are visible outside. Camera low from the rear seat, showing both men and the officer in one frame.",
