    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Lucien-17, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual image input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents; do not borrow its subjects or locations. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Lord Lucien [Cutout].webp` as Lord Lucien’s exact identity reference and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as post-Embrace Fomórach’s exact identity reference. Preserve their faces, apparent ages, builds, relative stature, hair, complexion, and distinguishing anatomy while adapting clothing and grooming to 1967–1980. Also attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Obfuscate Invisibility).png` and `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Mask of 1000 Faces).png` as visual-language references only.\n\nOBFUSCATE LANGUAGE — Use an Obfuscate effect only where a quad explicitly requests it. “Concealment” means Fomórach’s true form remains visible to the privileged audience, but selected contour regions dissolve into unfinished charcoal hatching and blank negative space borrowing the background texture, matching the Obfuscate Invisibility reference; keep most of him solid and recognizable, without a colored aura. “Mask” means his true form remains visible to the privileged audience while exactly one faint, translucent, ordinary human face and body are aligned over the same pose like a double exposure, matching the Mask of 1000 Faces reference; it is one superimposed perceptual shell, not a second person. Nearby mortals simply keep their attention elsewhere; do not build elaborate eyeline choreography around proving the effect.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1967–1980, Toronto, Canada. Lucien is an elegant, slim, blond Toreador rebuilding political standing through charm and ambition. Fomórach is a massive, severely deformed Nosferatu whose presence communicates the boon, protection, and complicated partnership behind Lucien’s arrival. Period Toronto moves from late-1960s brick and rail infrastructure toward 1970s towers and the CN Tower. All scenes are at night or within controlled sunless interiors. Every quad must depict both Lord Lucien and Fomórach. Clothing, vehicles, architecture, tools, and infrastructure must be period-appropriate.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe and render only what one camera can see in one instant. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful camera variation without obscuring anatomy or interaction. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in each quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, romantic posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn Union Station’s monumental concourse at night, Lucien is walking beside a luggage cart and is offering arrival documents to a station official with a polished, amused smile. Fomórach is walking at Lucien’s other side using Mask of a Thousand Faces: one faint ordinary railway porter’s face and coat are precisely superimposed over his true Nosferatu body, matching the same stride. Lucien is glancing toward Fomórach while the official studies the papers. Stone columns, cigarette haze, baggage carts, and sparse travellers establish the late 1960s. Use a wide eye-level camera with both men full-length.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a formal Camarilla receiving room, Lord Lucien and Fomórach are standing together on the far side of a large Toronto map-table across from Maximillian Steele, the severe bearded vampire official seated in profile at screen-right. Lucien is sliding a sealed petition across the map with one hand while keeping his body leaned forward; his head is turned screen-right and his eyes meet Maximillian's face with a confident, intent half-smile. Fomórach is standing openly without Obfuscate at screen-left, one broad hand resting on the back of an empty chair; his face is turned farther screen-right and slightly downward, his glowing eyes looking past Lucien and directly meeting Maximillian's face. Maximillian is looking back at Lucien with hands clasped near his mouth. Heavy furniture, guarded doors, controlled lamps, the supplied standalone Camarilla emblem, and restrained red route markers convey the Iron Praxis. Camera low at the table edge.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOn a wet Yonge Street at night in the mid-1970s, Lucien is shaking hands with a stylish nightclub manager beneath neon marquees while Fomórach is standing a few paces behind using concealment. His true body is visible to the audience, but charcoal hatching and negative-space fragments break his outline into the rain-dark storefront behind him. Lucien is smiling toward the manager while gesturing back toward Fomórach with his free hand, implying an unseen resource rather than inviting attention. Streetcars, period cars, brick façades, and restrained red neon recede toward new office towers. Use a slightly elevated street-corner camera.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nInside a temporary warehouse haven beside the rail corridor, Lucien and Fomórach are leaning over a Toronto map spread across a crate with no mortals present and no Obfuscate active. Lucien is moving a red marker toward Montreal with two fingers, his expression bright with dangerous ambition; Fomórach is holding Lucien’s wrist just above the map, his eyes narrowed and mouth tense in warning. Freight doors, pallets, an office cage, heavy curtains, and distant train light frame the conflict. Use an overhead camera tilted enough to show both faces and the map.",
