    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow, neutral black cross-shaped gutter to keep the four scenes visually separate; do not let figures, smoke, snow, architecture, or lighting cross between quads. Do not place letters, captions, borders around individual quads, logos, watermarks, or other readable text in the image, except for the single nightclub sign explicitly required in Quad A.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs to the generation call; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet and metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, locations, symbols, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Lord Lucien [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Lord Lucien; preserve his facial structure, blond curls, slim build, apparent age, and identity while dressing him appropriately for Montreal between 1980 and 1999. CHIMERSTRY VISUAL LANGUAGE — Establish a consistent supernatural shorthand distinct from Blood Sorcery. Chimerstry appears as soft, slightly luminous violet-purple smoke around the outer boundary of an illusion, while the interior of that smoky boundary depicts the illusion itself as a coherent, fully rendered scene. The smoke is a frame or threshold, not an opaque cloud hiding the illusion. For discrete illusionary people, duplicates, vehicles, structures, or other objects, render them completely and realistically but make their colors subtly brighter and more saturated than the real environment, with their silhouettes thinly limned by the same violet-purple vapor. Portions beginning to fail may unravel into that purple smoke. Never use red or crimson smoke for Chimerstry, and never depict it as skeins of light, blood magic, generic energy, or fog with nothing visible inside.\n\nCAMERA DIRECTION — Treat camera placement as an expressive tool rather than a default gimmick. Across a four-quad sampler, most concepts may use clear conventional cinematic framing, but one or two quads may use a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder view, foreground obstruction, or another unusual viewpoint where it materially intensifies danger, power, vulnerability, surveillance, speed, or disorientation. Do not force an unconventional angle into every quad. Avoid extreme fisheye distortion, novelty angles, broken anatomy, unreadable action, or compositions that sacrifice the calm overlay area. When a quad specifies an angle, honor it in the final image.\n\nAcross all four concepts, portray Montreal as the “Soul of the Sabbat”: snow-darkened old stone, Gothic churches, deindustrialized warehouses, biker compounds, neon nightlife, occult markings, cruel packs, predatory faces, occasional fangs, ritual scars, and selective deep-crimson eye-glow. Lucien is not a Sabbat infiltrator, convert, initiate, or willing participant in their rites. He is an openly opposed Camarilla rebel and valuable war asset using charm, Chimerstry, intelligence, and daring to disrupt Sabbat power. Lucien remains a slightly cocky charmer and charismatic socialite: in conversation give him an easy smile, amused half-smirk, expressive eyes, and confident gestures; in immediate danger keep him alert rather than sultry or posed. Every quad must depict active interaction and a different kind of contribution to the war effort. Chimerstry must not resemble blood sorcery: no blood threads, ritual circles cast by Lucien, sigils, magical beams, or generic energy from his hands. Keep a calm dark area within each composition for eventual time, location, and narrative overlays. No graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nUse the attached Lucien-19 composition sketch as the governing blocking map for this single frozen instant. The camera is positioned across the street at natural human eye level in a wide 16:9 view. A tall nightclub façade is filling the upper frame; the sidewalk and a narrow strip of wet street are running across the bottom. In the lower-left third, an open nightclub doorway is glowing dark red beneath a vertical red neon sign reading exactly “Croc-Rouge.”\n\nLord Lucien is standing immediately to the left of the bouncer at the doorway, wearing a chic dark winter coat over late-twentieth-century evening clothes. Lucien’s left hand is resting lightly on the bouncer’s near shoulder while his right hand is making one open, animated conversational gesture. His face is turned toward the bouncer, his eyes are meeting the bouncer’s eyes, and he is wearing an easy, slightly cocky smile. The bouncer is standing immediately to Lucien’s right in black leather with both hands planted on his hips, elbows spread. His torso and face are turned toward Lucien; he is looking directly at Lucien with a suspicious, severe expression, giving Lucien his full attention.\n\nExactly three real allied vampires are clinging to the building façade in the upper-right half of the image at three distinct heights. They are solid, opaque people in varied dark late-twentieth-century coats and practical clothing, each with a different silhouette. Their bodies are pressed to the vertical masonry as they are climbing diagonally downward and left toward the bouncer, with hands and feet braced against the wall. Their faces and eyelines are directed toward the bouncer and doorway. They remain spatially separated from Lucien and the bouncer and do not overlap the neon sign. This is a stealth approach captured at one instant; the allies are not illusions and no supernatural visual effect surrounds them.\n\nGentle snow is falling through the red neon and streetlight. Wet black pavement, thin snowbanks, old stonework, and a few period-appropriate parked cars are establishing wintertime Montreal. The primary focal interaction is Lucien calmly holding the bouncer’s attention while the three allies descend unseen above and to the right.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nUse a high-angle view from the Gothic church's choir loft, looking down across Lucien, the charging rebels, and the violet-smoke-framed false wall as it opens; preserve clear faces, readable action, and the apparent depth of the revealed passage. During a Camarilla raid on the desecrated church, Lucien pushes through the snowy doorway and exposes a hidden Sabbat escape passage by breaking a Chimerstry concealment. The false stone wall remains fully visible inside the boundary of slightly luminous violet-purple smoke, while the center of that smoky frame peels open to reveal the real passage and fleeing war pack. Armed Camarilla rebels surge toward the revealed route as gaunt Sabbat vampires with fangs and crimson eye-glow recoil among overturned pews, black candles, biker jackets, and corrupted devotional art. Lucien points out the real fugitives with a fierce, confident half-smile; the failing portions of the false wall dissolve into purple vapor rather than red smoke or magical energy.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a clandestine Camarilla safehouse loft overlooking a snowbound Montreal skyline, Lucien is caught mid-briefing as he slaps photographs, coded notes, and a marked city map onto a crowded war table. His cocky, magnetic smile holds the attention of operatives already pulling on winter coats, checking weapons, and moving toward the door. Through industrial windows, old church spires, neon streets, and smoke over the river suggest the Sabbat city they are preparing to strike. Above the map, a small Chimerstry reconstruction appears inside an oval boundary of slightly luminous violet-purple smoke: the interior of the smoke clearly depicts a complete, brighter, more saturated miniature view of a Sabbat biker compound and its patrol routes. This makes Lucien's intelligence value immediately visible without portraying him as an infiltrator or ritual participant.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a deindustrialized biker stronghold beside the frozen Lachine Canal, Lucien leads a fast Camarilla sabotage raid through blowing snow. Sabbat bikers with ritual scars, occasional fangs, and selective red eye-glow fire toward convincing illusionary duplicates and a phantom police assault, while the real rebels seize weapons, documents, and fuel from another side of the compound. The decoy people, vehicles, and searchlights are fully rendered but slightly brighter and more saturated than reality, with their silhouettes thinly limned by soft violet-purple smoke; failing edges unravel into that same purple vapor. Lucien moves with coat flaring, directing allies toward the intelligence cache. Motorcycles, corrugated warehouses, chain-link fences, old church towers, and red neon in the distance make this unmistakably Montreal's brutal Sabbat underworld.",
