    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-13, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Aishe Tache [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Doran [Cutout].webp` as exact identity reference for Prince Doran; preserve that character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1865–1911, New Orleans, United States. Aishe is an ageless vampire after her Embrace: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads even when the depicted decade changes. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nOn a Reconstruction-era river landing at night, abandoned Aishe bargains for passage with a suspicious riverboat captain while vigilantes search the levee behind her. Cheap luggage, a weathered shawl, muddy flood marks, freed laborers, gamblers, and lanternlit cargo surround her. She palms a stolen deck of playing cards and quietly redirects the search toward another gangplank, showing improvised survival and social cunning rather than courtly power.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn the cellar of an abandoned farmstead beyond New Orleans, Aishe kneels beside an unnamed escaped criminal she has just fed from and discovers a plain deck of cards among his possessions. Use a close over-the-shoulder view as she turns the Emperor card toward a shaft of moonlight; the card’s shadow points impossibly toward the distant city. Keep the omen restrained and physical, with no colorful spell effects, while danger from riders and dogs approaches outside.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn Prince Doran’s Creole court, Aishe presents herself before the hopeful prince while hostile Camarilla courtiers close ranks around him. Prince Doran leans forward to test her claim; Aishe places the Emperor card on the polished floor between them and answers with unnerving confidence. Guards, petitioners, old gaslight, and a blood-price ritual waiting behind screened doors convey that admission will cost something terrible. Use a low angle from the card’s level to make the negotiation feel momentous.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nNear the opening of Storyville, Aishe conducts a theatrical reading for Prince Doran and a semicircle of politicians, performers, reformers, and Kindred petitioners in her newly established occult salon. Electric light competes with candles; a streetcar flashes past wet windows. Aishe delivers a riddle with a knowing half-smile while quietly sliding a decisive card toward Doran, showing how performance, genuine prophecy, and court influence have become inseparable.",
