    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-18, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Aishe Tache [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Doran [Cutout].webp` as exact identity reference for Prince Doran; preserve that character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1911–1931, New Orleans, United States. Aishe is an ageless vampire after her Embrace: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads even when the depicted decade changes. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a polished prewar oracle salon, Aishe stands at the head of a crowded reading table and abruptly rearranges the seating of rival petitioners before Prince Doran enters. Her Tarot cards, mirrors, and red flowers create a controlled stage; courtiers, suffragists, businessmen, and artists react as alliances are exposed by where she places them. Prince Doran watches from the doorway, recognizing that Aishe is governing the room through apparent whimsy.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAt the World War I riverfront at night, Aishe intercepts Prince Doran beside a troop embarkation line and thrusts a single card beneath his gaze while soldiers, nurses, stevedores, and military police move around them. A distant ship, blackout precautions, and secured cargo frame the argument. Aishe points toward one doomed loading operation; Doran must decide whether to trust a prophecy that risks Masquerade exposure. Use a tense, compressed viewpoint through stacked crates.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside an influenza emergency ward in 1918, masked nurses struggle among crowded beds while Aishe catches a desperate vampire courtier reaching toward a feverish patient. She blocks the feeding with one arm and uses the other to redirect a doctor toward a patient whose survival she has foreseen. The composition should show Hunger, plague, compassion, and Masquerade danger in one active moment, with harsh electric lamps and deep red limited to medical markings and blood-dark shadows.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nDuring the Great Mississippi Flood of 1927, Aishe and Prince Doran argue over a relief map on the deck of a rescue boat while floodwater swallows streets behind them. Aishe points toward stranded families and a failing levee; Doran gestures toward guarded Camarilla assets and supplies. Refugees, relief workers, armed officials, and floating debris force political ideals into immediate moral choices. Use a high angle from the boat’s upper deck to reveal the scale without turning the scene into a landscape-only image.",
