    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-22, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Aishe Tache [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Doran [Cutout].webp`, `assets/references/npc-character-references/Marcel Guilbeau [Cutout].webp` as exact identity references for Prince Doran and Marcel Guilbeau; preserve each character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1931–1955, New Orleans, United States. Aishe is an ageless vampire after her Embrace: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads even when the depicted decade changes. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nWARDROBE AND STAGING SAFEGUARD — Depict every character as a fully dressed adult in conservative, historically appropriate public or formal clothing, with high necklines and ordinary coverage. Frame all interactions as public, professional, political, investigative, or civic. No romance, seduction, intimacy, bedroom staging, exposed undergarments, or sensual posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nDuring the Great Depression, Aishe conducts a private reading for Prince Doran in the back room of a relief kitchen while unemployed families queue beyond a thin partition. Doran studies municipal ledgers and relief tokens; Aishe turns over a card whose shadow falls across both the soup line and a locked Camarilla strongbox. Their active disagreement should contrast his hopeful politics with her growing distrust of promised prosperity.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAt a secured New Orleans shipyard during World War II, Aishe moves through blackout darkness with a port-security officer and catches an unnamed saboteur or spy reflected in a rain puddle before the guards see him. She points sharply while workers scatter and a military vessel looms beyond the fence. Searchlights, ration crates, identification badges without readable text, and red warning lamps make prophecy useful amid wartime surveillance without depicting overt magic.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a postwar jazz room used for a covert civil-rights meeting, Aishe deals Tarot across a piano while organizers, veterans, younger Kindred, and police informants watch one another. She abruptly hands one organizer the key to a rear exit as a raid begins outside, turning foreknowledge into protection. Early television glow, electric fans, segregated street life beyond the windows, and restrained red stage light place the scene in the changing late 1940s or early 1950s.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn 1955, Aishe stands beside an empty ornate chair in a grand Creole court gone unnaturally still as Marcel Guilbeau advances to claim authority. She holds up one warning card between Marcel and the assembled courtiers while servants extinguish candles behind her. Marcel’s triumph is measured and political; Aishe’s grief is controlled but unmistakable. Marcel must match only the attached `assets/references/npc-character-references/Marcel Guilbeau [Cutout].webp` identity reference: a younger adult man with shoulder-length dark hair, short beard and stubble, sharp blue-eyed features, and a lean build. Do not blend his face, hair, age, grooming, or physique with any other reference. No other named male character appears in this quad. Use a low, slightly off-center angle that frames the vacant chair as the true absence governing the scene.",
