    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-10, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Black Caesar [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; beside standing adult men, the top of his head and shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Jervais de la Croix [Cutout].webp` as the identity reference for Jervais de la Croix; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being communicated only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining intelligible without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All concepts are taking place within 1752–1789, ports and sailing ships across the Atlantic, Indian, and Pacific oceans. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. Every exterior is taking place at night or in storm-darkness and every interior is excluding direct sunlight. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms with softened lower bodies, drifting edges, and the recognizable faces and period clothing of the dead.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The alternatives are exploring meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, stature, and focal interaction. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nOn the moonlit deck of an eighteenth-century armed sailing ship, Black Caesar is standing on the lower quarterdeck and is extending one straight arm toward a locked cargo hatch on the enemy vessel alongside. His eyes are fixed on the hatch, his brows are drawn down, and his mouth is open in a concise command. Crewmen are crossing taut grappling lines between the two ships while one sailor is bracing a boarding plank. Cannon smoke is drifting low across torn rigging without obscuring Caesar's short, compact silhouette. The camera is positioned behind a coil of rope at deck level, looking upward only slightly so the hatch, Caesar's pointing arm, and the boarding route form one clear diagonal.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a storm-rocked captain's cabin at night, Jervais de la Croix is sliding a sealed order and a palm-sized iron chest across a chart table toward Black Caesar. Jervais is looking directly at Caesar with chin lifted and lips pressed into a cold line. Caesar is standing alone on the opposite side of the table, visibly shorter than Jervais, with one hand braced on the table edge; he is looking up into Jervais's eyes with narrowed eyes and a tight, challenging mouth. Route maps and captive manifests are lying flat beneath the two objects, and a guarded hatch is visible behind Caesar. The camera is low behind stacked ledgers at the table corner, placing the order, the chest, and the two men's opposing eyelines on one diagonal.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a humid Indian Ocean harbor warehouse at night, Black Caesar is holding a sealed metal reliquary at chest height toward a taller customs officer across a weighing table. Caesar's eyes are fixed on the officer, one eyebrow is raised, and his mouth is set in a knowing half-smile. The officer is recoiling slightly with one open palm raised and is staring at the reliquary with widened eyes. Two sailors are standing several paces behind Caesar beside stacked ritual cargo, watching the officer rather than posing with Caesar. Open warehouse doors are showing dark water and moored sailing ships. The camera is over the officer's shoulder, making the reliquary, Caesar's clean-shaven face, and their difference in height dominant.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nOn the final Pacific approach toward New South Wales in 1789, Black Caesar is standing alone at the ship's wheel on a raised helmsman's platform beneath a violent black night sky. One hand is gripping the wheel while his other hand is pulling several clean, glowing red-white lines of energy away from an iron-bound occult crate lashed near the mast. The energy is appearing as distinct luminous strands, not webbing, and is breaking into sparks between his fingers and the crate. Caesar's red-lit eyes are fixed on the strands, his teeth are clenched, and wet curls are whipping across his clean-shaven face. Two generic sailors are bracing ropes on the lower deck while a pursuing naval lantern is glowing through rain astern. The camera is low beside the crate, looking along the energy lines toward Caesar and the wheel.",
