    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-13, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Black Caesar [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; beside standing adult men, the top of his head and shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. \n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being communicated only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining intelligible without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All concepts are taking place within 1789–1796, the early colonial settlement at Sydney Cove, New South Wales. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. Every quad is unmistakably taking place after sunset, under a dark night sky or inside a lamplit room with black windows. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms with softened lower bodies, drifting edges, and the recognizable faces and period clothing of the dead.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The alternatives are exploring meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, stature, and focal interaction. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt Sydney Cove beneath a deep-black night sky in 1789, Black Caesar and a generic adult sailor are standing knee-deep beside a crowded launch at an unfinished timber dock. Caesar is gripping one end of a heavy ration crate while the sailor is gripping the other; Caesar's compact body is visibly shorter. Caesar is looking past the crate toward a marine guard with narrowed, calculating eyes, while the sailor is looking at Caesar for direction with a tense, attentive expression. Lantern-lit tents, rough huts, storehouses, tethered boats, convicts, and marines are forming the fragile settlement behind them. The camera is at water level beside the launch, with the crate in the foreground and Caesar's small stature clearly visible.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a ration store after sunset, Black Caesar is planting the point of a period knife through a false tally slip beside a tampered brass weight on the counter. He is looking up at a taller quartermaster across the counter with a level stare, lowered brows, and a closed, unsmiling mouth. The quartermaster is leaning backward and staring down at the pinned paper with widened eyes. A generic store clerk is standing behind the quartermaster beside an open hidden sack of grain, looking anxiously toward the knife. Caesar's head is visibly lower than both men. Convicts and soldiers are watching through a doorway opening onto complete darkness. The camera is high above one corner of the counter, centering the knife, false weight, and opposing eyelines.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nAt a punishment ground under a black night sky, Black Caesar is holding an official seal at eye level toward a marine officer who is standing beside a bound escaped convict. Caesar is shorter than both men but is holding his shoulders square. His eyes are fixed on the officer, his brows are lowered, and his expression is coldly expectant. The officer is staring at the seal with a reluctant frown while his hand is hanging motionless beside a discarded lash. Two generic sailors from Caesar's crew are standing several paces behind him, watching the officer without drawing focus. Torches, timber palisades, distant huts, and silent convicts are surrounding the confrontation. The camera is low behind the discarded lash, directing the eye upward toward the seal.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nOn a bush track beyond Sydney Cove under clouded moonlight, Black Caesar is crouching between colonial soldiers and Aboriginal scouts and is pointing toward a plume of smoke and a shadowed figure moving between trees. Caesar's lowered pistol is resting across his other forearm. His eyes are fixed on the distant movement, his brows are raised, and his lips are parted in a quiet warning. Both separated groups are turning their faces along Caesar's pointing arm toward the same distant threat while keeping their weapons lowered. The camera is overhead on a restrained Dutch angle, showing Caesar's compact body between the two groups and the single shared eyeline leading into the dark landscape.",
