    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-19, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter must separate the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Black Caesar [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar; preserve his facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, short stature, apparent adult age, and completely clean-shaven face in every quad. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Jean Ducheski-Francois I (Pre-Death) [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Jean Ducheski I. The reference is showing Jean alive; every quad is instead depicting him after death as a cold ash-grey translucent wraith with the same recognizable Black facial structure, apparent age at death, dark eyes, and period sailor's clothing. Attach `assets/output/memoriam-splashes/samplers/Black Caesar/pass-3/black-caesar-19-four-quad-sampler.png` only as a composition reference. Use only that reference image's bottom-left quad as the spatial model: a cramped wooden shipboard cabin, a rectangular mirror on the left wall, Black Caesar immediately to the mirror's right near a floor veve, and a dramatic high three-quarter viewpoint. Its other three quads are irrelevant, and its missing second ghost is not part of the desired content.\n\nSAMPLER PURPOSE — All four quads are depicting variations of the same single frozen shipboard ritual. Each variation must show exactly three supernatural-story figures: Black Caesar in the cabin, Jean Ducheski I standing directly behind him with both spectral hands resting on Caesar's shoulders, and one entirely different wraith visible only inside the mirror. Jean is not the mirror ghost. The mirror ghost is not emerging into the room. The alternatives are testing camera placement and blocking while preserving the bottom-left composition reference's mirror-left, Caesar-centre-right geometry.\n\nCORE STAGING — The sealed shipboard cabin has black night beyond its shutters. A large flowing Voodoo veve is drawn across the floorboards, with a small iron reliquary resting at its center and restrained red-white lines of Blood Sorcery lifting from its seams. Black Caesar is kneeling or half-crouching just outside the veve and is extending one open palm toward the rectangular mirror on the left wall. His eyes are fixed on the different wraith inside the mirror; his brows are lowered, his jaw is tight, and his expression is commanding. Jean's ash-grey translucent body is standing immediately behind Caesar. Both of Jean's spectral hands are visibly resting in firm contact with Caesar's two shoulders, and Jean is looking past Caesar toward the mirror with fierce concentration. A pale grey-white current is flowing only from Jean's palms into Caesar's shoulders and arms. Inside the mirror glass, the second wraith has a clearly different face, body, and clothing from Jean and is recoiling beneath Caesar's outstretched hand.\n\nVISUAL RULES — Each quad is one decisive still image, not a synopsis, montage, or sequence. Wraiths are cold ash-grey translucent human forms with drifting edges and recognizable period clothing. Jean must match the attached identity reference; the compelled mirror wraith must look unmistakably different. The mirror contains only the second ghost's reflection and never Jean's. Jean remains physically behind Caesar in the room with both hands touching Caesar's shoulders. Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean red-white lines, a veve, and restrained luminous contours rather than webbing. Render the cabin, clothing, mirror, lanterns, and ritual objects accurately for 1846–1871. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. No additional people or spirits, captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nClosest match to the attached pass-3 bottom-left composition: the camera is high in the cabin's rear-right corner at a three-quarter downward angle. The rectangular mirror fills the left wall. Short Black Caesar is kneeling immediately to its right, outside the flowing floor veve, with one open palm held toward the glass and his commanding gaze fixed on the different wraith contained inside it. Jean Ducheski I is standing directly behind Caesar, fully separate from the mirror, with both translucent hands planted on Caesar's left and right shoulders. Jean's recognizable referenced face is angled toward the mirror, his brows drawn down in concentration. Pale grey-white energy is travelling from Jean's palms into Caesar; restrained red-white ritual light is rising from the reliquary at the veve's center. The mirror wraith is visibly recoiling and has a different face and clothing from Jean.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nThe camera is positioned low beside the iron reliquary at the center of the floor veve, looking upward across the red-white ritual lines. Short Black Caesar is half-crouching beyond the reliquary and is extending one open palm toward the rectangular mirror on the left wall. His eyes are locked on the second wraith inside the glass, his brows are lowered, and his mouth is set in command. Jean Ducheski I is standing immediately behind Caesar with both ash-grey spectral hands resting in clear contact on Caesar's shoulders. Jean's face matches the attached identity reference and is looking over Caesar's head toward the mirror with fierce concentration. The mirror contains one different ghost with an unfamiliar face and different clothing, recoiling behind the glass. Jean's body is entirely outside the mirror.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nThe camera is positioned just beside the left edge of the rectangular mirror, looking diagonally across the cabin. The different mirror wraith occupies the near portion of the glass and is recoiling with widened eyes; its face and clothing are clearly unlike Jean Ducheski I. Immediately to the mirror's right, short Black Caesar is kneeling outside the floor veve and is holding one open palm toward the ghost, his eyes fixed on it and his expression sternly commanding. Directly behind Caesar, Jean's recognizable ash-grey wraith is standing with both hands visibly gripping Caesar's shoulders. Jean is staring at the mirror ghost with clenched concentration while a pale current is entering Caesar through both shoulder contacts. The veve and iron reliquary remain visible below them in restrained red-white light.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nThe camera is positioned above and slightly behind Black Caesar's right shoulder, preserving the mirror-left composition while making all four hands readable. Caesar's open right palm is extending toward the rectangular mirror, where one unfamiliar wraith is confined inside the glass and is shrinking backward from his command. Caesar's face is visible in three-quarter profile, with narrowed eyes fixed on that ghost and a tense jaw. Jean Ducheski I is standing directly behind Caesar; Jean's face matches the attached reference, and both of his translucent hands are resting symmetrically on Caesar's shoulders. A pale grey-white current is flowing from those two hand contacts into Caesar's arms. The large floor veve and its central iron reliquary occupy the lower frame with restrained red-white light. Jean and the mirror wraith remain visibly separate people.",
