    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-21, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no figures, architecture, smoke, weather, ships, or lighting crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, text, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Black Caesar [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; when he is standing beside other adult men, the top of his head and his shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Jervais de la Croix [Cutout].webp` as the identity reference for Jervais de la Croix; preserve the referenced face, apparent age, complexion, build, hair, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing and grooming to the depicted decade.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a scene summary, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being shown only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining understandable without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All four concepts are taking place within 1871–1880, Reconstruction-era St. Augustine, United States. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. Every exterior is taking place at night or immediately after twilight; every interior window and open doorway shows complete darkness outside. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Ghosts and wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms, breath-like mist, or displaced shadows.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The four alternatives are using meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, and the focal interaction. Named figures are remaining visually distinct and sufficiently separated. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt a Reconstruction-era St. Augustine dock beneath a dark indigo night sky, Black Caesar is standing beside a cargo agent who is pausing with an iron-bound crate on a handcart. Caesar is visibly shorter than the agent and is pointing toward a particular warehouse marked only by a red lantern. His eyes are fixed on the agent, his brows are raised, and his mouth is slightly open in a precise correction. The agent is following Caesar's pointing hand with a chastened expression. Freed workers, veterans, telegraph poles, modest hotels, weathered coquina walls, and a schoolhouse are visible under sparse gaslights. The camera is looking past the crate from handcart height, placing Caesar's pointing arm and the red lantern on the same diagonal.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside Black Caesar's polished office at night, Jervais de la Croix is extending a small signet across a desk toward Caesar. Jervais is looking down at him with formal reserve and a faintly tightened mouth. Caesar is visibly shorter and is reaching toward the signet with one hand while keeping his other palm firmly on an open shipping ledger; he is looking up into Jervais's eyes with a guarded, unsmiling expression. Two visiting occult officials and one servant are standing well behind Jervais as silent witnesses. The tall window beyond them is showing only black night and a few distant gaslights. The camera is low behind stacked ledgers at the desk corner, making the signet, Caesar's hands, and the two men's eyelines the entire focal triangle.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOutside a freedpeople's school immediately after twilight, Black Caesar is standing between a local sheriff and three armed white vigilantes while teachers are guiding children through a side gate behind him. The last post-sunset sky is dark indigo with no direct sunlight. Caesar is shorter than the sheriff and vigilantes and is holding one official paper at the sheriff's eye level. His eyes are fixed on the sheriff, his brows are lowered, and his mouth is closed in controlled defiance. The sheriff is reading the paper with a reluctant frown while one vigilante is staring past him with jaw clenched. A teacher is looking back toward Caesar while keeping one hand on a child's shoulder. The camera is over a vigilante's shoulder, making Caesar's small stature and immovable position visually central.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nInside a dockside warehouse at night, an ash-grey wraith is suspended above a large flowing Voodoo veve painted on the floor. Black Caesar is standing clearly outside the veve, visibly shorter than the two adult assistants behind him. Several clean red-white lines of energy are rising from the veve and coiling tightly around the wraith's wrists, torso, and ankles. Caesar is extending one open hand toward the spirit while looking directly into its face; his brows are knitted and his lips are parted as he is questioning it. The wraith is leaning against the luminous restraints with its mouth open and eyes fixed on Caesar. Black merchants, clergy, sailors, and one revenant assistant are waiting behind marked thresholds. The open doorway and windows show complete darkness. The camera is low beside the edge of the veve, angled upward through the energy lines toward Caesar and the wraith.",
