    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-27, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Black Caesar [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; beside standing adult men, the top of his head and shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Carna [Cutout].webp` as the identity reference for Carna; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Terence Merik [Cutout].webp` as the identity reference for Prince Terence Merik; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Mortius [Cutout].webp` as the identity reference for Mortius; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being communicated only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining intelligible without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All concepts are taking place within 1912–1930, Milwaukee, United States. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. Every exterior is taking place at night or in storm-darkness, and every interior excludes direct sunlight. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms with softened lower bodies, drifting edges, and the recognizable faces and period clothing of the dead.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The alternatives are exploring meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, stature, and focal interaction. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt Milwaukee's wooded industrial edge beneath a snow-dark night sky, Black Caesar is standing low and compact at the centre of a failing red-white geometric ward, pressing both palms toward its fractured lines. His clean-shaven face is turned toward the breach, his teeth are clenched, and his eyes are wide with concentration. Carna is standing behind him on the left, pointing defenders toward one opening while looking along her arm with a sharp commander's stare. Prince Terence Merik is standing on the right, visibly taller than Caesar, bracing a bent iron gate with both hands while staring at a huge werewolf silhouette partly obscured by trees and factory smoke. The camera is low behind broken ward-stones, making Caesar's short stature, the three coordinated eyelines, and the single breach immediately readable.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a shattered chantry corridor, short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is crouching and pulling wounded Apprentice Mortius backward by the shoulders away from a narrow gap beneath a descending iron door. Caesar's eyes are fixed on Mortius, his brows are drawn down, and his mouth is open in a forceful command. Mortius is reaching one hand toward a dropped ritual book lying just beyond the door while staring at it with a desperate, pained expression. Large werewolf claws are reaching through the narrowing gap behind the book. A glowing red ward is tracing the doorframe. The camera is resting on the floor beside the book at a low Dutch angle, so the book, Mortius's reaching hand, Caesar's compact body, and the claws occupy one clear line.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside an overwhelmed Milwaukee clinic during the 1918 influenza crisis, short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is gripping the wrist of a gaunt vampire whose open mouth is inches above an unconscious patient's neck. Caesar is looking directly into the vampire's face with lowered brows and bared teeth, holding the feeding arm away from the patient. Carna is standing on the opposite side of the bed, holding a cloudy glass medicine vial toward an electric lamp while staring at a black-red residue inside it with narrowed eyes. Masked nurses, crowded cots, undertakers, and stacked medical crates are filling the background. The camera is directly above the patient's shoulder, making the restrained wrist, Caesar's eyeline, Carna's vial, and the vulnerable patient one frozen crisis.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nInside a Prohibition-era Milwaukee lakefront speakeasy at night, an overturned table is forming cover across the foreground. Short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is crouching behind it and pointing one arm toward a dark rear service exit; his eyes are fixed on Prince Terence Merik and his mouth is open in a concise order. Merik is kneeling taller beside him and is looking toward the front entrance where police silhouettes are visible through frosted glass. Mortius is crouching on Caesar's other side, clutching route maps and watching the indicated rear exit with tense, widened eyes. Seized liquor ledgers and a lakefront map are scattered behind the table. The camera is positioned just beyond the front doorway at boot height, using broken glass and chair legs as foreground obstruction while keeping all three faces readable.",
