    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-29, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, ships, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Black Caesar [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar; preserve his facial structure, dark skin, powerful build, apparent adult age, and commanding presence while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/output/character-intro-splashes/candidates/Black Caesar/black-caesar-lwa-possession.png`, an existing present-night title-credit asset, only as a structural reference for legible spirit possession or Lwa intervention; do not copy its exact pose, setting, or composition.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1936–1998, Montreal, Canada. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period; preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. Adapt ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport to the specific decade and geography of each quad. Caesar is a disciplined survivor, mariner, occult operative, and later commander: depict him actively navigating, bargaining, fighting, directing, studying, or choosing—not passively posing. Treat slavery, colonial violence, famine, war, and racial oppression with gravity rather than adventure-romance. Blood Sorcery may appear as restrained geometric skeins or seals of deep-red light. Ghosts, wraiths, and Lwa should appear as cold ash-grey translucence, shadow, breath-like mist, or possession expressed through a host’s body; do not use Chimerstry’s purple smoke language or generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen danger, command, confinement, or surveillance. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, triumphalist colonial imagery, pirate caricature, or glossy superhero posing. Keep named characters sufficiently separated for readable interaction. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a Depression-era Montreal House Goratrix vault, newly arrived Caesar challenges a circle of Sabbat war leaders over a map of Camarilla territory. He drives a dagger into one route while pack members, occult researchers, and armed couriers react. Snow-dark brick, Gothic church foundations, rail tunnels, and deep-red ritual geometry establish genuine commitment to the Sabbat rather than a disguised infiltration.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nDuring wartime harbor security, Caesar directs a Sabbat raid through blackout-dark warehouses while military patrols search the docks. He uses forged orders to divert soldiers, then signals vampires through a service tunnel toward occult cargo. Cranes, convoy ships, ration crates, winter fog, and restrained red lamps place supernatural warfare inside 1940s Montreal without making every scene ritual-centered.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nDuring the Quiet Revolution or October Crisis era, Caesar commands a covert council in a deconsecrated church while bikers, intellectuals, militants, and House Goratrix researchers argue around him. Metro construction and modern concrete rise beyond old stained glass. Caesar tears down an obsolete clan decree and replaces it with a tactical plan, showing the mortal city and his wartime leadership changing together.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn 1998, the global antitribu purge strikes Caesar inside a late-century ritual command room. Other Tremere antitribu collapse as deep-red wards rupture across computers, grimoires, and stone walls; an ash-grey Lwa throws itself around Caesar as a protective possessing shadow and is torn apart by the blast. Caesar reaches toward it in horror while surviving the catastrophe. The event fills one quarter only; it must not overwhelm the period’s other three environments.",
