    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-1, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 historical splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its characters, locations, symbols, words, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Pre-Embrace).jpg` as the exact identity reference for late-teen Fomórach. Preserve his clearly youthful facial structure, bright red hair, tall stature, sturdy build, and late-teen appearance; do not age him into an older adult.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts during Fomórach's mortal emigration from Belfast to the East Coast Colonies in the late eighteenth century. Architecture, clothing, tools, ships, market goods, and colonial infrastructure are accurate to the period and geography. Fomórach is being depicted as an observant, stubborn, physically sturdy late teenager who is learning to survive by listening carefully, testing claims, and helping fellow travelers. His intelligence is being shown through specific attention to a person, ledger, scale, hatch, or ration store.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is showing one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis or sequence. Every featured person has one principal pose or action, one explicit eyeline, and one visible expression. Narrative meaning is being carried by bodies, positions, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle's high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Vary the four camera geometries where useful while preserving readable anatomy, youthful age, stature, expressions, eyelines, and focal interaction. Treat poverty, migration, difficult contracts, sectarian pressure, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve one calm, dark, low-detail region in every quad for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic injury, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy hero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn daylight outside a crowded Belfast family home, adolescent mortal Fomórach is placing a small cloth purse containing his inheritance into his father's open palm. His father is still gripping the lead rope of the family's final cow with his other hand and is staring at the purse with lowered brows and a tight, conflicted mouth. Fomórach's eyes are fixed on his father's face; his jaw is set and his shoulders are squared despite his youth. A ship recruiter is waiting one pace away with a folded indenture contract held against his coat, watching silently rather than touching Fomórach. Younger siblings are clustered in the doorway beside linen, carpentry tools, and a damaged Catholic devotional object. The camera is at natural eye level and wide enough to show that Fomórach is tall for seventeen but still unmistakably adolescent.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a busy Belfast marketplace near the harbor, adolescent mortal Fomórach is pinning one hand firmly against the pan of a merchant's false weighing scale, stopping it from moving. His other hand is holding a simple honest tally board beside the fraudulent weight for immediate comparison. Fomórach's face is turned toward the ship agent across the stall; his eyes are narrowed, one eyebrow is raised, and his lips are pressed into a skeptical challenge. The agent is recoiling slightly with one hand hovering above the scale, eyes darting toward two laborers who are now watching the exposed mismatch. Canvas stalls, linen goods, carts, tavern fronts, church spires, and ship masts are filling the background. The camera is positioned just above the tabletop so the two measures, Fomórach's youthful face, and the agent's reaction are all clearly visible.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOn the wet deck of an emigrant ship in heavy Atlantic weather, adolescent mortal Fomórach is crouching low beside a loose deck grating with one ear angled toward two officers speaking above it. His eyes are fixed upward toward their boots and shadows, brows knitted in concentration, while one hand behind his back is making a small pointing gesture toward two hidden water casks for the huddled passengers sheltering near the guarded hatch. A wave is breaking over the far rail, rigging is straining overhead, and passengers are pressed together under rough canvas. The camera is low at deck level through ropes and spray, keeping Fomórach's adolescent proportions, listening posture, single covert signal, and the officers' elevated position readable in one frozen instant.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a struggling East Coast colonial outpost at night, late-teen Fomórach is pausing with both hands gripping a wooden supply crate beside raw cabins and a muddy work yard. His face and eyes are turned toward an official who is inspecting an overturned ration barrel under lantern light; Fomórach's brows are lowered and his lips are slightly parted in wary concentration. The taller official is comparing a nearly empty grain scoop with a closed supply ledger while two exhausted workers wait nearby. The black forest, crude palisade, abandoned tools, unfinished cabins, and scattered provisions create a tense picture of a settlement running out of food. The camera is at crate height and wide enough to preserve Fomórach's late-teen appearance and tall, sturdy scale against the adults.",
