    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-5, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Pre-Embrace).jpg` as Fomórach’s exact pre-Embrace identity reference. He is seventeen at his 1786 Embrace: preserve his unmistakably adolescent face, bright red hair, tall-for-his-age stature, and sturdy build; never depict this version as an adult man. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as his exact post-Embrace identity reference; follow the mortal/Embrace instruction below for which version appears in each quad. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Drake [Cutout].webp` as exact identity reference for Drake; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1786–1793, the failing East Coast colonies. The period crosses ghouldom and Embrace: keep Fomórach recognizably the same seventeen-year-old adolescent while making the transition from mortal hardship to the visibly inhuman curse of his Nosferatu blood unmistakable. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nQUAD-SPECIFIC IDENTITY LOCK — Quads A, B, and C depict only pre-Embrace Fomórach using the human reference: an ordinary living human face and anatomy, with no Nosferatu deformities, corpse pallor, fangs, glowing or predatory red eyes, or other vampiric traits. Ghouldom in Quads B and C affects only his endurance, deprivation, and craving; it does not alter his human appearance. Only Quad D may begin the transition toward the post-Embrace Nosferatu reference and visible deformities.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nInside the communal store of a failing East Coast colonial settlement, newly arrived adolescent mortal Fomórach is standing at a rough table between an open ration ledger and an almost empty grain bin. He is holding a full measuring scoop beside the ledger's much larger written tally, making the mismatch visible without relying on readable text. His eyes are fixed on the senior Puritan official opposite him; Fomórach's brows are raised and his mouth is set in a blunt, challenging line. The taller official is leaning back with arms folded, chin lifted, and eyes narrowed dismissively toward the Catholic servant. Two laborers are watching the mismatched scoop and bin from the doorway. Fresh cabins, unfinished fields, muddy tools, and dense forest are visible outside. The camera is level with the tabletop so the evidence and Fomórach's unmistakably youthful face share the focal plane.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nFrom a listening-wall viewpoint inside a rough frontier tavern, ghouled but still fully human-looking adolescent Fomórach is kneeling beside split timber with one ear pressed to a narrow crack. Through the crack, officials, hunters, and preachers are visible around a candlelit table. Fomórach's eyes are lowered in concentration, his face deliberately slack and unremarkable, while one hand beneath the floorboards is passing a small carved token into a single dark-wrapped hand reaching up from Drake's hidden hatch. Fomórach's body remains separated from Drake. The camera is close beside the wall, making the listening posture, token exchange, and oblivious officials part of one readable frozen instant.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a snowbound winter storehouse, starving ghouled but still fully human-looking adolescent Fomórach is extending the last wooden bowl of thin food toward a delirious settler seated beside an empty shelf. His arm is trembling and his cheeks are gaunt, but his eyes are fixed intensely on a small covered vessel of vampire blood sitting untouched on a separate stool behind the settler. His brows are drawn upward with strain, his jaw is clenched, and one bead of sweat is visible despite the cold. Frost coats the walls, abandoned tools lie under failing lantern light, and accusations from a crowd outside are suggested by silhouettes and raised lanterns beyond the shuttered door. The camera is at bowl height so the offered food, forbidden vessel, and Fomórach's adolescent face form one clear line.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nUse a first-person point of view through Drake's eyes immediately after the Embrace, looking steeply down at seventeen-year-old Fomórach lying beneath him in fresh snow beside a ruined frontier shelter. Drake himself is not a visible standing figure; at most, the extreme lower edge contains one indistinct dark-wrapped forearm. Fomórach is lying on his back in torn late-eighteenth-century frontier clothing, his unmistakably adolescent face staring upward in shock while one empty hand reaches weakly toward the viewer. Two small clean fang marks are visible at the side of his neck. Branching black veins are spreading beneath his pallid skin from those marks like ink corruption or frost cracks, beginning the Wendigo curse and the transition toward his later Nosferatu form. Snow is falling through moonlight and gathering on his bright red hair, shoulders, broken timbers, and dead leaves. The transformation is localized and readable rather than grotesque, with no open wound or graphic gore.",
