    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-8, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Drake [Cutout].webp` as Drake’s exact appearance reference: his identity remains deliberately unknowable, with his face, head, and skin completely obscured by the same dark wraps in every depiction; never render him bare-faced or conventionally human-looking. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Maximillian Steele [Reference].png` as Maximillian Steele’s exact identity reference; preserve Steele’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting his costume and grooming to the period. Attach `assets/output/character-intro-splashes/candidates/Fomórach/fomorach-listening-wall.png`, an existing present-night title-credit asset, only as a composition reference; do not copy its exact setting, figures, or props.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1793–1846, York and early Toronto, Canada. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period: preserve the reference identity, severe deformity, powerful frame, and apparently starved, predatory physicality across all four quads. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt the 1793 lakeshore founding of York during a deep moonless night, Fomórach and Drake are crouching below a rough timber survey platform while soldiers and laborers are marking road lines above by shielded lantern light. The sky is nearly black, with no dawn, daylight, or bright blue twilight. Fomórach is pressing one ear to the newly dug earth and pointing one clawed finger toward a natural drainage cut descending from the shoreline. His eyes are fixed on Drake, brows lowered with urgent concentration. Drake's fully wrapped face is turned toward the indicated cut, one dark-wrapped hand resting on a rolled survey sheet. Fort timbers, garrison boats, tavern frames, Indigenous trade canoes, and the muddy lakeshore are visible only in pools of lantern light and cold silver moonlight. The camera is low within the drainage cut, looking slightly upward while preserving the black night sky.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nDuring the Battle of York in 1813, the scene is taking place at night beneath a black, smoke-choked sky with no daylight or bright twilight. From a restrained Dutch angle inside a collapsing cellar, Fomórach is bracing one heavy timber beam across his shoulders and raised arms while civilians are crawling beneath it toward an escape tunnel. His head is turned toward the ruptured street opening, and his glowing eyes are fixed on soldiers carrying one locked strategic chest past the opening; his mouth is tense and his posture is straining between rescue and intelligence. Drake is remaining deeper in shadow beside the tunnel mouth, his wrapped face and one open hand angled toward the escaping civilians. Firelight, dim lake-gun flashes, falling dust, and shielded lanterns provide the only illumination. The camera is low behind a broken cellar stair, keeping the collapsing beam, fleeing civilians, chest, and Fomórach's exact eyeline readable in one frozen instant.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn 1818, Fomórach accompanies Drake to an austere court audience before Iron Prince Maximillian Steele. Steele points to a city plan and demands hidden access beneath the growing settlement; Drake bargains calmly while Fomórach notices an eavesdropper behind the paneling and silently blocks their escape. The scene should make the Iron Praxis feel like a political settlement built atop Nosferatu knowledge.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nBy the late 1830s, Fomórach and Drake are standing at a broad underground worktable beneath Toronto at night. Several large architectural blueprints are spread flat across the table, clearly depicting tunnels, cellars, drains, hidden doors, and concealed access routes beneath the growing city. Fomórach is holding out one massive iron key ring crowded with many large keys of different shapes and lengths; his eyes are fixed on Drake's wrapped face, his chin is raised, and his mouth is set with hard-earned confidence. Drake is receiving the heavy ring with one dark-wrapped hand while his other hand rests on the blueprints; his obscured face is angled down toward the keys. An open brick sewer arch behind them reveals only a black night sky, wet street lamps, horse-drawn traffic, market buildings, and layered cellar entrances above. The camera is positioned just above the blueprint table so the secret routes fill the foreground and the key ring is unmistakably a collection of access keys rather than jewelry or merchandise. No market stall, watches, coins, or small trinkets.",
