    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-15, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Its characters, locations, symbols, words, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach; preserve his severe Nosferatu deformity, powerful frame, gaunt predatory physicality, apparent age, and recognizable identity while adapting clothing to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1846–1849, Belfast and London, United Kingdom. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth are reading through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, sharpened fangs, and restrained red accents without glamourized feeding.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is showing one decisive instant in one location. Every featured person has one principal pose or action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative meaning is being communicated only through bodies, spatial relationships, physical props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle's high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder views, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen grief, rage, judgment, confinement, or forced transport while preserving readable anatomy and eyelines. Treat famine, dispossession, violence, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. The complete sampler contains no montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or monster pin-up posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn rain at night, Fomórach is kneeling inside the roofless ruins of his poor ancestral Belfast home during the Great Famine, holding one surviving gold crucifix and rosary carefully in both hands. His amber eyes are fixed on the cross; his jaw is clenched and his hunched shoulders turn grief toward rage. The stone fireplace at screen-left is cold, soot-black, rain-damp, and completely unlit, holding only gray ash and collapsed charred wood. The debris consists solely of burned and looted remnants of a humble rural homestead: splintered crude pine table and stool pieces, broken plain earthenware, a cracked iron pot, torn coarse wool, scorched straw ticking, a collapsed rough shelf, bent simple utensils, and blackened homespun cloth. The gold crucifix is the sole intact object of value. Distant estate agents search the rain by weak lantern light. Use a low three-quarter camera just inside the ruined doorway.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a gaslit London rookery, Fomórach hurls an exploitative landlord or agent through a lodging-house doorway while terrified tenants scatter and police lanterns close from both ends of the alley. Use a low, restrained Dutch angle through broken furniture to capture the beginning of his bloody campaign. Keep victims and violence largely obscured; grief curdling into indiscriminate vengeance is the subject.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a hidden London Nosferatu court, Fomórach is standing in the center of the chamber under heavy physical restraint. Thick iron manacles are locked around both wrists and both ankles; four short chains are pulled taut from those manacles to separate iron rings bolted into the stone floor and walls, forcing his arms outward and limiting every step. The chains are visibly functional restraints, not necklaces, belts, draped accessories, or clothing. Fomórach is leaning forward against the taut chains with bared teeth, his glowing eyes fixed on an unmasked gaunt Nosferatu judge seated across an evidence table. The judge is watching him with chin lowered and lips compressed. Burned favor tokens, maps, and sealed complaints cover the table while other sewer-dwellers stand behind it. The camera is low beside one floor bolt, using the taut chain in the foreground to lead directly to Fomórach's restrained wrists, furious face, and the judge's eyeline.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a fog-dark railway freight warehouse, the camera is positioned just inside the foot of an open wooden coffin and is looking upward along Fomórach's rigid body. A thick wooden stake is visibly embedded through the center of his chest over his torn clothing, its shaft rising vertically from him; both of Fomórach's hands are lying open and empty at his sides, far from the stake. His eyes are closed and his body is completely motionless. An unmasked, pale-haired London Nosferatu official with an exposed gaunt face is leaning over the coffin and pressing a wax seal onto the outer crate. This official has no dark facial wraps and does not resemble Drake. Two ordinary freight workers are securing ropes around the crate while rain, steam, rails, and departure machinery fill the background. The camera keeps the embedded stake, Fomórach's empty hands, the official's unwrapped face, and the transport preparations unobscured, with no blood or graphic injury.",
