    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-23, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Its characters, locations, symbols, words, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, preserving his severe Nosferatu deformity, powerful frame, gaunt predatory physicality, apparent age, and recognizable identity while adapting clothing to the period. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Oksana 'Mara' Ziva (Pre-Embrace) [Cutout].webp` as Oksana's exact mortal identity reference. Preserve her human facial structure, apparent age, build, complexion, and distinguishing features while adapting her clothing and grooming to 1930s Ukraine.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1932–1936, Kharkiv and the surrounding Ukrainian countryside. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout. Oksana remains a living human woman in every quad, including Quad D at the instant immediately before Fomórach bites her; she has ordinary human facial proportions, human eyes, human teeth, and no Nosferatu changes. Architecture, clothing, tools, rail equipment, weapons, institutions, and infrastructure are accurate to the decade and geography. Fomórach is being shown as a covert observer and dangerous selector; Oksana is being shown as active, defiant, physically depleted, and difficult to control. Obfuscate reads through swallowed light and impossible shadow rather than colorful invisibility effects.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is showing one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis or sequence. Every featured person has one principal pose or action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative meaning is being carried by bodies, positions, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle's high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Vary camera geometry where it strengthens surveillance, hunger, resistance, or the fatal choice while preserving readable anatomy, expressions, and eyelines. Treat the Holodomor and state-created deprivation with historical gravity rather than picturesque ruin. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. The complete sampler contains no montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or romanticized feeding.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt a guarded grain rail siding during the Holodomor, Fomórach hides beneath a freight platform and listens as officials divert food away from starving villages. He reaches through shadow to steal a manifest token while soldiers pass within arm’s reach. Empty carts, sealed grain, smoke, snow, and distant civilians establish state-created deprivation; do not turn hunger into picturesque ruin.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn an overwhelmed Kharkiv clinic, Fomórach watches Oksana Mara Ziva refuse her own ration so another patient can eat. She remains active and defiant despite starvation, arguing with an official while helping a child or elder stand. Fomórach studies her from a service corridor, recognizing endurance and rage rather than selecting a passive victim.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOn an abandoned farm at night, Oksana Mara Ziva catches Fomórach testing her with a concealed food cache and turns a weapon on him instead of taking the bait. He steps from Obfuscate-shadow with empty hands, impressed, while informants and predators search the road beyond. Use a low threshold viewpoint to emphasize mutual suspicion, hunger, and the dangerous logic of his selection.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nInside a sealed rail warehouse at night, mortal Oksana Mara Ziva is standing with her back pressed against stacked grain sacks while Fomórach restrains her from the side. Oksana's head is being pulled sharply away from him, her chin lifted and turned toward the camera so the full side of her bare neck is exposed. Her eyes are wide, her brows are drawn upward, her jaw is clenched, and both of her hands are pushing against Fomórach's forearm rather than touching his face. Fomórach's mouth is open beside the exposed side of her neck, with his fangs clearly visible and stopping within an inch of the skin at the frozen instant before the bite. His eyes are fixed only on her neck. Their mouths are far apart and their faces are not aligned for a kiss. Oksana still looks completely human, using only her pre-Embrace reference: no deformity, fangs, red eyes, or other vampiric changes. Locked grain doors, iron bars, cold warehouse lamps, and distant soldiers visible only through the barred exterior doors are framing the scene. The camera is slightly below shoulder height and close enough to make the exposed neck, approaching fangs, Oksana's resisting hands, and both eyelines unmistakable without blood or graphic injury.",
