    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Fomórach-24, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, supernatural effects, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual image input. Use `assets/output/memoriam-splashes/samplers/Fomorach/fomorach-24-four-quad-sampler.png` as the exact edit target: preserve its four compositions and all successful content. Use `assets/references/composition-references/Re Fomorach-24.jpg` only as an annotated correction guide: cyan circles identify pale curls that must be erased in Quads C and D; pink boxes identify the correct Mask of a Thousand Faces double-exposure structure for Quad B. Do not reproduce any circles, boxes, arrows, labels, or other markup. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as Fomórach’s exact post-Embrace identity reference. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach (Mask of 1000 Faces).png` only as a power visual-language reference. Use `assets/references/npc-character-references/Yusuf 'Palis' bin Yafa (Pre-Embrace) [Cutout].webp` as Yusuf’s exact mortal identity reference; preserve that identity as his first restrained transformation begins in Quad D.\n\nEDIT SCOPE — This is a tightly constrained correction of the existing sampler. Change only the Mask-of-a-Thousand-Faces rendering in Quad B and the pale ear wisps in Quads C and D. Preserve Quad A exactly. Preserve the established framing, figures, poses, eyelines, settings, lighting, palette, period detail, panel boundaries, and black gutters in all four quads.\n\nMASK OF A THOUSAND FACES — In Quad B, Fomórach’s actual monstrous body is the solid foundation: 100% opaque, dark, sharply defined, physically present, and fully readable from face through suit and body. Exactly one anonymous human disguise is superimposed over that same body as a faint translucent double-exposure shell at roughly 25–35% opacity. Align the human shell’s head, shoulders, torso, and limbs directly with Fomórach’s corresponding anatomy, with only a tiny offset sufficient to let both faces remain readable. Only the human disguise is ghostly; Fomórach is never transparent, faded, spectral, or made of smoke. The overlay is not a separate person standing beside or behind him.\n\nEAR AND HEAD SURFACES — In Quads C and D, erase every pale white curl, wisp, tendril, filament, halo, or smoke-like ornament around Fomórach’s ears and the back of his skull, especially at the exact cyan-circled locations in the annotated guide. Replace those artifacts with uninterrupted matte charcoal-gray leathery scalp and ear skin, plus adjacent dark background or coat where anatomically appropriate. His bald deformed head must have a clean solid silhouette. These areas are skin and shadow—not hair, horns, smoke, magic, aura, or decorative anatomy. Quads C and D contain no Obfuscate visual effect.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1945–1951, Jaffa. Fomórach is a massive, severely deformed Nosferatu vampire. Yusuf is mortal in A–C and newly Embraced only in D. Treat war, displacement, and refugee life with gravity. Every quad occurs at night or inside a sunless shelter.\n\nSTYLE — Preserve the current sampler’s cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, and restrained blood-red accents. No captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermark, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nOn a damaged Jaffa port street at night, Fomórach is carrying a wooden crate of bandages against his chest while using concealment: most of his true monstrous form is solid and recognizable to the audience, but his shoulders, coat edges, and legs are dissolving into dense charcoal hatching, fine visual noise, and fragments of the broken stone street directly behind those contours. Yusuf is several paces ahead, pointing a field medic toward an open cellar shelter while looking toward frightened civilians moving through the doorway. Fomórach is watching Yusuf with narrowed, appraising eyes. Sailors, aid workers, damaged carts, shuttered homes, and distant gunfire flashes establish the conflict without spectacle. Use a low camera behind the medical crate.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside the existing crowded clinic and refugee shelter, preserve Yusuf, the military official, their poses, the room, and the current camera exactly. Correct only Fomórach’s Mask of a Thousand Faces depiction behind Yusuf. Fomórach’s massive Nosferatu body, deformed face, glowing eyes, dark suit, shoulders, torso, arms, and hands are all 100% opaque, solid, dark, sharp, and physically present. Exactly one nameless middle-aged human aid worker in rolled sleeves is superimposed directly over Fomórach as a faint 25–35%-opacity double-exposure shell. The human face is aligned over Fomórach’s face, the human shoulders over his shoulders, and the human torso and limbs over his identical pose, with only a tiny lateral offset so both identities can be read. The anonymous human is the sole translucent element. Fomórach is not translucent or ghostly, and the human shell is not a separate background figure. Fomórach is looking toward Yusuf’s defiant posture.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nPreserve the existing Quad C composition exactly: Yusuf is holding the key ring and folded list while facing Fomórach at the damaged stone threshold, and Fomórach is pointing toward the patrol lights. Correct only Fomórach’s head surface. At the cyan-circled area around his ear and rear skull in the annotated guide, every pale white curl, wisp, tendril, filament, halo, and smoke-like mark is completely erased. The corrected area is uninterrupted matte charcoal-gray leathery scalp and ear skin with a clean bald silhouette, blending naturally into the adjacent dark background and coat. There is no hair, smoke, magic, aura, horn, or Obfuscate effect around his head.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nPreserve the existing Quad D composition exactly: newly Embraced Yusuf is gripping Fomórach’s forearm in the sealed harbor room while Fomórach supports him. Correct only Fomórach’s head surface. At the cyan-circled area around his ear and rear skull in the annotated guide, every pale white curl, wisp, tendril, filament, halo, and smoke-like mark is completely erased. The corrected area is uninterrupted matte charcoal-gray leathery scalp and ear skin with a clean bald silhouette, blending naturally into the adjacent dark background and coat. There is no hair, smoke, magic, aura, horn, or Obfuscate effect around his head.",
