    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-27, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Fomórach [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Drake [Cutout].webp` as Drake’s exact appearance reference: his identity remains deliberately unknowable, with his face, head, and skin completely obscured by the same dark wraps in every depiction; never render him bare-faced or conventionally human-looking. Adapt only his outer clothing to the period while preserving the dark wrappings. Attach `assets/output/character-intro-splashes/samplers/Fomórach/pass-2/fomorach-path-command-center-variations-sampler.png`, an existing present-night title-credit asset, only as a composition reference; do not copy its exact setting, figures, or props.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1967–1998, Toronto, Canada. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period: preserve the reference identity, severe deformity, powerful frame, and apparently starved, predatory physicality across all four quads. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn 1967 beneath active subway construction, Fomórach reports a completed cross-country delivery to Drake while workers drill through the wall beyond their hidden chamber. Drake demands terms of the inherited boon; Fomórach places car keys and travel papers on the table, then points to new tunnels the city has accidentally opened. The scene should show return, reckoning, and immediate reintegration into the undercity.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a 1970s transit service tunnel, Fomórach races beside a stalled train and tears open an access panel to divert smoke and guide trapped commuters toward an emergency exit while Camarilla agents search another platform for a hidden intruder. Fluorescent light, raw concrete, streetcar and subway infrastructure, and red emergency lamps make rescue, sabotage, and feeding territory overlap.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn an 1980s telecommunications room, Fomórach catches a hacker or Sabbat infiltrator tapping clan lines. He pins the cable beneath one claw, listens through a headset, and signals ghouls to close physical routes while screens and relay racks pulse around him. Use a high angle through bundled cables so the undercity’s evolution from brick tunnels to an intelligence network is visually clear.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn a hidden late-1990s Toronto operations room where rail, sewer, steam, electrical, surveillance, and early digital systems converge, Fomórach is commanding two human field agents before a bank of six CRT surveillance screens. There is no map: the central workbench holds analog control panels, rotary knobs, toggle switches, indicator lamps, coiled cables, telephones, radio equipment, and plain monitoring logs. Fomórach's screen-right arm is extended upward with one index finger pointing at a CRT screen. His other forearm crosses low in front of his torso and reaches screen-right, its open hand sweeping the two operatives toward the exit beyond the right edge. His head and glowing eyes are turned toward the humans as his mouth opens in command. Both operatives are shown from behind taking urgent first running steps screen-right. Drake remains motionless and fully wrapped at screen-left, silently observing. Use a high, slightly oblique camera over the control workbench.",
