    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-4, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Rashid Abdulrahman [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below. Attach `assets/references/npc-character-references/Laleh bint Saif [Cutout].webp` as exact identity reference for Laleh bint Saif; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1811–1818, intact but militarizing Diriyah. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a concealed safehouse in 1811, Laleh bint Saif completes Rashid’s Embrace and initiation into the Web of Knives. Rashid rises from the floor already reaching for the coded message beside him while Laleh stops him from opening the door onto his former family street. A restrained red blood seal, covered water basin, weapons, and prayer niche convey lineage, loss, and immediate duty without sensuality or gore.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nFrom a rooftop above Diriyah’s fortified market, Rashid and Laleh bint Saif track an Ottoman courier moving through the crowd. Rashid signals hidden agents by shifting laundry and lanterns while Laleh watches his discipline. Watchtowers, supply yards, palm groves, family streets, and desert approaches show the capital tightening under war without yet becoming ruins.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a Warrior Caste compound, Rashid undergoes an interrogation exercise: bound at the center of a red geometric ward, he identifies the real infiltrator among masked trainers by noticing who reacts to a coded phrase. Laleh bint Saif observes from behind a screen, neither rescuing nor praising him. The scene should emphasize spycraft, clan doctrine, and the pressure to treat certainty as virtue.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nNear 1818, Rashid stands over a military map in a supply yard and insists that assassinating one hidden Kindred ruler could break the enemy’s coordination. Laleh bint Saif points to alliances and civilian routes he has ignored, but Rashid closes the discussion and takes his weapons. Use a low angle through stacked spear shafts to show confidence hardening into the decision that will destroy the city.",
