    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Rashid-6, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Rashid Abdulrahman [Cutout].webp` as Rashid’s exact identity reference. Use `assets/references/npc-character-references/Ibrahim Kethüda [Cutout].webp` and `assets/references/npc-character-references/Laleh bint Saif [Cutout].webp` as exact identity references. Use `assets/output/character-intro-splashes/candidates/Rashid/rashid-containing-catastrophe.png` only as a composition reference for disciplined containment under pressure. Preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, complexion, hair, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing and grooming to 1818. Character identity references override other references.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1818, fallen Diriyah. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire. Laleh’s uncovered skin is uniformly supernatural, light-absorbing black with no mortal undertone. With the sole exception of the controlled sunbeam striking Ibrahim in Quad A, every scene is night. Rashid must never be touched by direct or reflected sunlight. In Quad A his face remains uncovered and recognizable, but his entire body and face are safely enclosed within deep architectural shadow behind a thick wall; the sunbeam never reaches him. Architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice suit the decade and geography.\n\nSUPERNATURAL CHRONOLOGY — Ur-Shulgi’s Promise has not yet burned Rashid during this period. In every quad, the ring may be visible but Rashid’s ring-bearing finger, other fingers, palm, and hand all retain ordinary unburned skin. There is no blackened flesh or red supernatural glow on his hand. Blood Sorcery appears as disciplined geometric skeins, incomplete calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral blood memory appears as one coherent scene inside a red-black threshold.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe only one camera-visible instant per quad. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear anatomical expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful low, high, over-the-shoulder, or architectural viewpoints without obscuring anatomy. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in every quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, static lineup posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt sunrise inside a shattered palace, Prince Ibrahim Kethüda is lying immobilized on the bright side of a stone threshold while a narrow, fiercely overexposed shaft of direct sunlight is striking across his body. Ibrahim’s head is thrown backward, his eyes are squeezed shut, his mouth is stretched wide in a raw scream, and the muscles in his neck, shoulders, and outstretched arm are rigid with agony. Dense white-gray smoke is pouring from his exposed skin and streaming from every opening and fold of his clothing, surrounding him in blast-furnace heat haze as cloth edges curl and buckle. His recognizable face remains visible through the smoke.\n\nRashid is crouching far behind the thick interior wall at screen-left in a completely black recess. His face is uncovered and fully recognizable in the cool reflected darkness, but his skin and body remain entirely inside absolute architectural shadow. He is pulling a long shutter rope around the wall; the rope alone crosses the light. Rashid’s eyes are fixed on Ibrahim, his brows raised and jaw clenched. Use a side-on doorway composition that makes the protected dark chamber and the white-hot sunlit room two physically separate zones. No visible flames, wounds, gore, or disfigurement.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAt night in a firelit street of fallen Diriyah, Rashid is standing on a collapsed stair and pointing civilians toward an intact alley with one extended arm. His ash-streaked face is tense and his eyes are fixed on a family below. His other hand is clearly visible with an ordinary ring on a completely normal, unburned finger and hand. Occupation troops, stripped palms, prison lines, wounded walls, and distant fires reveal the catastrophe around him. Use a high view from a broken watchtower, keeping the sky unmistakably dark.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nAt night among the ashes of a family courtyard, Laleh bint Saif is kneeling beside shrouded dead and raising one open palm toward Rashid in a final stopping gesture. Her skin is uniformly supernatural black and absorbs the surrounding firelight; her lips are pressed closed and her eyes are fixed on Rashid with grief and accusation. Rashid is kneeling several paces away with both hands open, explanation halted. Rashid’s ordinary unburned ring, broken household objects, and one sealed clan message lie between them. Use a low camera beside the ring.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a torchlit occupation checkpoint outside ruined Diriyah at night, Rashid is leaning over a rough table and is placing one intelligence map beneath the hand of a foreign officer. His eyes are fixed on the officer, expression controlled and exhausted. Behind Rashid, Laleh bint Saif—her skin uniformly supernatural black—is standing among rescued prisoners beside a concealed caravan, one hand resting on a child’s shoulder. The officer’s guards are watching the map. Weapons, chains, pack animals, and black sky frame the bargain. Use an over-the-shoulder view from behind the officer.",
