    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Rashid-7, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Rashid Abdulrahman [Cutout].webp` as Rashid’s exact identity reference. Preserve his face, apparent age, build, complexion, hair, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing and grooming to 1819–1839.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1819–1839, Alamut, Afghanistan. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire. All exterior scenes are at night. Several truly ancient Banu Haqim vampires appear in the sampler; their uncovered skin is uniformly supernatural, light-absorbing black with no mortal undertone. Younger vampires may retain natural mortal complexions. Architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice suit the specific decade and geography.\n\nSUPERNATURAL CHRONOLOGY — Ur-Shulgi’s Promise has not yet burned Rashid during this period. In every quad, the ring may be visible but Rashid’s ring-bearing finger, other fingers, palm, and hand all retain ordinary unburned skin. There is no blackened flesh or red supernatural glow on his hand. Blood Sorcery appears as disciplined geometric skeins, incomplete calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe only one camera-visible instant per quad. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful low, high, over-the-shoulder, or architectural viewpoints without obscuring anatomy. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in every quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, static lineup posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt night in Alamut’s torchlit judgment hall, Rashid is standing alone below ordered stone tiers and is placing Ibrahim Kethüda’s broken alliance tokens on the floor beside his ring-bearing hand. That hand and every finger are completely normal and unburned, with the ordinary ring visible against natural skin. His head is raised toward the judges, his eyes are steady, and his mouth is tense. Three ancient judges with uniformly supernatural black skin are seated above younger warriors, scribes, and servants. Use a low viewpoint beside the evidence, with the black mountain sky visible through narrow arches.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nDeep inside a windowless mountain library, Rashid is pinning one manuscript page beneath his ring-bearing hand while a censor’s fingers are reaching for its edge. Rashid’s hand and every finger are completely normal and unburned, with the ordinary ring visible against natural skin. His eyes are fixed on the source register in the censor’s other hand and his brows are drawn in precise challenge. Shelves, oil lamps, stone passages, scribes, and guarded doors surround the contested page. One ancient librarian in the background has uniformly supernatural black skin. Use an over-the-shoulder view from behind the censor.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a snow-dusted training yard beneath moonlight and torches, Rashid is holding a supervising warrior’s lowered blade aside with one forearm while pointing his ring-bearing hand toward a bound prisoner. The pointing hand and every finger are completely normal and unburned, with the ordinary ring visible against natural skin. Rashid is looking directly at the supervisor, jaw set in argument; the prisoner is watching Rashid with guarded hope. The ancient supervisor’s uncovered skin is uniformly supernatural black. Younger clan factions are observing from the stone arcade. Use a slightly elevated diagonal view; the sky is fully night.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt Alamut’s guarded mountain gate at night in 1839, Rashid is placing a returned clan insignia into the open palm of an ancient official whose skin is uniformly supernatural black. Rashid’s ring-bearing hand and every finger are completely normal and unburned. His other hand is gripping the strap of a pack filled with books; he is looking past the official toward the moonlit road with exhausted resolve. Messengers with new orders are arriving behind the portcullis. Frame through the iron bars so the open night road and closed institution divide the image.",
