    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Rashid-12, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents; do not borrow its subjects or locations. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Rashid Abdulrahman [Cutout].webp` as Rashid’s exact identity reference.  Preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, complexion, hair, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing and grooming to 1893–1901. Character identity references override the style reference.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1893–1901, Alamut, Afghanistan. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire. Every quad occurs at night or inside a completely windowless chamber. Ancient clan vampires have uniformly supernatural, light-absorbing black skin with no mortal undertone; younger vampires may retain natural complexions.  Architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice must suit the specific decade and geography.\n\nSUPERNATURAL LANGUAGE — Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is a blackened ring and finger on Rashid’s hand, glowing restrained deep red only under supernatural pressure. Blood Sorcery appears as disciplined geometric skeins, incomplete calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral blood memory appears as one coherent scene inside a red-black threshold, never purple smoke or generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe only one camera-visible instant per quad. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful low, high, over-the-shoulder, or architectural viewpoints without obscuring anatomy. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in every quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, static lineup posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt Alamut’s gate beneath moonlight and torches, Rashid is holding a sealed blood sample against his chest while an ancient gate official with uniformly supernatural black skin is extending an open hand for it. Rashid’s blackened ring remains visible on the hand gripping his travel case; his eyes are fixed on the official and his mouth is set in refusal. Younger armed guards, snow, pack animals, telegram cases, old stone, and modern rifles frame the inspection. Use a low view from the table edge; the sky is fully night.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a windowless ritual library, Rashid is tracing one missing segment in a hovering deep-red calligraphic diagram with his ringed finger while an ancient sorcerer with supernatural black skin is holding back a loose manuscript page against his chest. Rashid is looking directly at the concealed page, brows narrowed in recognition. Two younger scribes watch from the shelves. Oil lamps and disciplined red geometry illuminate the stone room. Use a close over-the-shoulder camera behind the sorcerer.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a circular windowless testing chamber, Rashid is kneeling with his ringed palm pressed to the stone floor, drawing several unstable blood-memory fragments into one coherent red-black threshold. His teeth are clenched and his eyes are fixed on the converging geometry. Ancient judges with uniformly supernatural black skin are watching from high balconies while one younger rival stands at the circle’s edge. Use a high overhead angle; keep the memory images small and subordinate to Rashid’s control.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt Alamut’s mountain gate at night in 1901, Rashid is placing a ceremonial blade into the hands of an ancient official whose skin is uniformly supernatural black, while scholarly trunks wait behind him on pack animals. Rashid’s blackened ring remains exposed; he is looking toward two waiting couriers on the moonlit road with settled resolve. One restrained red glow leaks through a trunk seam. Frame from inside the portcullis toward the black night beyond; no dawn light.",
