    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-18, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/references/pc-character-references/Rashid Abdulrahman [Cutout].webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1922–1952, multiple deliberately anonymous European locations. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn an interwar Continental archive, Rashid corners an émigré collector who has forged a sighting of Laleh. He compares old clan seals beneath a desk lamp, quietly locks the door as police enter the lobby, and takes only the one authentic address fragment. Avoid recognizable national landmarks; architecture, clothing, files, and exhaustion should support many European cities.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAt a 1930s international railway border, fascist officers inspect Rashid’s changing papers while another traveler is pulled from the queue. Rashid uses a reflected red glimmer from his ring to notice an informant signaling from the platform, then switches luggage tags and sends a threatened family toward a different train. Use a compressed viewpoint through carriage windows to emphasize surveillance and moral risk.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nDuring wartime occupation, Rashid meets smugglers, refugees, and an occult informant in the service corridor of an anonymous hotel while soldiers raid the rooms above. He holds a door against collapsing debris, points civilians toward the kitchen exit, and forces the informant to reveal that the latest sighting is false. Blackout curtains, ration cards without readable text, uniforms, and red emergency light keep the setting broadly Continental.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn a postwar refugee and transit camp, Rashid finally receives a credible Atlantic lead among mountains of displaced records. He helps an exhausted clerk rescue files from rain, recognizes Laleh’s old cipher in one damaged entry, and turns immediately toward a departing train. Tents, ruined station architecture, aid workers, veterans, black markets, and uncertain borders close three decades of false trails with restrained hope.",
