    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 Memoriam splash concept sampler for Rashid-21, divided into four exactly equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: A top-left, B top-right, C bottom-left, D bottom-right. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter. Each quad is one independent frozen instant; figures, architecture, smoke, and lighting remain inside that quad.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Use `assets/references/style-references/general-style-reference-contact-sheet.png` only for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmosphere, dynamic composition, and restrained blood-red accents; do not borrow its subjects or locations. Use `assets/references/pc-character-references/Rashid Abdulrahman [Cutout].webp` as Rashid’s exact identity reference. Also use `assets/references/npc-character-references/Laleh bint Saif [Cutout].webp` as Laleh bint Saif’s exact identity reference. Preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, complexion, hair, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing and grooming to 1952–1997. Character identity references override the style reference.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set every quad within 1952–1997, Toronto, Canada. Rashid and Laleh are ageless Banu Haqim vampires. Laleh’s uncovered skin is uniformly supernatural, light-absorbing black with absolutely no mortal undertone. She does not appear undisguised in public. Every quad is set at night or inside a sealed sunless haven.  Architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice must suit the specific decade and geography.\n\nSUPERNATURAL LANGUAGE — Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is a blackened ring and finger on Rashid’s hand, glowing restrained deep red only under supernatural pressure. Blood Sorcery appears as disciplined geometric skeins, incomplete calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral blood memory appears as one coherent scene inside a red-black threshold, never purple smoke or generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Describe only one camera-visible instant per quad. Give each featured figure one principal pose, a clear expression, and a simple readable eyeline. Explore useful low, high, over-the-shoulder, or architectural viewpoints without obscuring anatomy. Reserve a calm dark low-detail area in every quad for later overlay text. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermark, anachronisms, static lineup posing, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nInside a locked, disused baggage office deep within Union Station at night in the early 1950s, Laleh bint Saif is standing across the room from Rashid and is raising one familiar silent hand signal. Her skin is uniformly supernatural black, absorbing the single shaded desk lamp; her face remains calm and severe. Rashid is frozen beside a frosted interior window, eyes widened toward her and blackened hand half-raised in recognition. Empty baggage cages, steam pipes, snow-darkened glass, and one closed service door keep the reunion private. Use a long lens through the bars of a baggage cage.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside Laleh’s concealed Toronto haven at night, Rashid and Laleh are seated across a bare judgment table. Laleh’s skin is uniformly supernatural black; she is placing one Diriyah token at the table’s center while holding Rashid’s gaze in absolute silence. Rashid is exposing the blackened ring on his open palm, expression controlled but wounded. Martial tools, ritual shelves, immigrant-street lights behind blackout mesh, and guarded doors frame the reckoning. Use a low table-level camera with the two objects between them.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nAt night in the 1970s or 1980s inside an industrial Toronto training room, Laleh—her skin uniformly supernatural black—is holding Rashid’s wrist at the end of a redirected knife exercise. Rashid’s free hand is pointing toward a wall map of clan contacts and occult leads, his eyes fixed on one marked route rather than the blade. Laleh is watching his stance with narrowed appraisal. Early computers, fax equipment, security monitors, and waterfront lights beyond heavy mesh show the haven becoming an intelligence center. Use a side-on camera at shoulder height; no daylight.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nInside a secure Toronto archive at night in the 1990s, Rashid is pinning two mismatched wax seals beneath a narrow red examination light while Laleh points one black fingertip at the repeated flaw. Her skin is uniformly supernatural black and her eyes are fixed on the seals. Rashid is looking at the same flaw, lips parted in realization. Contradictory dossiers, security glass, waiting chairs, and Toronto tower lights establish institutional infiltration without showing any alleged culprit. Use an overhead camera angled enough to show both faces and the evidence.",
